=F0=9F=93=8C IDEA OF THE DAY
AI protocol platform for functional medicine =
practitioners
February 24, 2026

Functional health practitioners love the =
detective work. Cross-referencing labs, connecting symptoms, finding the =
root cause. What they hate is the three to four hours of admin that =
follows: building supplement stacks, writing lifestyle protocols, and =
formatting everything into a plan a client can follow. Every practitioner =
builds protocols in isolation. The field runs on intuition when it could =
run on data.

Protocol Pad takes client labs, symptoms, and health history and generates =
a personalized treatment protocol: supplement dosages with timing, diet =
recommendations, follow-up testing schedules, and lifestyle interventions =
grounded in functional medicine frameworks. Practitioners adjust and refine=
. Client outcomes get tracked. Every protocol generated and every outcome =
logged feeds a clinical intelligence layer that surfaces which stacks =
produce the best results for similar lab profiles and symptom clusters. The=
 AI stops filling templates and starts recommending what works, backed by =
anonymized data from across the platform.

Build a web dashboard where practitioners upload client data and choose =
from evidence-based protocol templates trained on functional medicine =
literature and clinical guidelines. Integrate with supplement databases =
like Fullscript or Emerson Ecologics so dosing is accurate and ordering =
flows directly from the protocol. The regulatory positioning matters from =
day one: every output must frame the platform as a practitioner tool that =
assists clinical decisions, not one that prescribes them. Ship to 10 =
practitioners drowning in protocol work and let them stress-test with real =
clients before expanding the template library.

Solo practitioners pay $49/month to save time. Pro at $149/month adds =
outcomes tracking, client portals, and access to the clinical intelligence =
layer. Supplement companies pay for anonymized prescribing pattern data. =
Research institutions license the outcomes dataset. Distribution starts =
through functional medicine Facebook groups where practitioners already ask=
 for this kind of tool, and partnerships with organizations like the =
Institute for Functional Medicine reach thousands of practitioners through =
certification programs.

